The angle-to-speed correlation is presented as if it is a universal standard, but wind sock calibration varies. Not all socks are calibrated to 15 knots full extension — some airports use different calibrations. This should be noted as typical but variable.
The statement 'open end points in direction wind is blowing toward' is incorrect. Wind blows FROM one direction TO another; the open end faces the FROM direction (wind source).

