The FAA considers an approved MEL to be a Supplemental Type Certificate (STC) for that specific aircraft. Practically, this means the MEL is a legal document specific to that tail number that authorizes operations with certain equipment inoperative under defined conditions and procedures. You may only use an MEL that has been approved for your specific aircraft — you cannot apply another operator's MEL to your helicopter.

Revised Answer:
You may only use an MEL that has been approved for your specific aircraft — you cannot apply another operator's MEL to your helicopter. Practically, this means the MEL is a legal document specific to that tail number that authorizes operations with certain equipment inoperative under defined conditions and procedures. 

