Answer (at time of rejection):
Nuclear power plants are designated as National Security Areas (NSAs) or have established TFRs/prohibited areas protecting them. Under 14 CFR 91.141 and associated NOTAMs, flight over or near nuclear facilities may be restricted. During preflight planning, you must: (1) Check current NOTAMs and sectional charts for any TFRs, NSAs, or prohibited areas in proximity to the facility. (2) Identify any altitude restrictions that apply. (3) Review 14 CFR 99.7 for special security instructions. (4) Modify the route to maintain at least a safe lateral distance — typically a minimum of 2,000 feet AGL and 3 miles lateral from nuclear facilities is recommended by the NRC unless a specific restricted distance is published. (5) Brief all crew members on the rerouting and reason. Operating too close to such facilities without authorization can result in intercept, certificate action, and federal prosecution.

