Verifier Notes:
Reference to 'Squawk 7600 if radio communication is lost' is contextually misplaced — this answer discusses a scenario where radio communication with ATC is active and the pilot is requesting clarification. Squawk 7600 (Lost Communications code) is used when two-way radio communication with ATC has been lost entirely, which contradicts the scenario where the pilot is requesting progressive taxi. The answer should clarify this distinction.

