Immediately deviate to one side of the runway centerline — helicopters have the unique advantage of being able to maneuver laterally while climbing. Fly to the runway edge or off the runway edge corridor, climb aggressively if terrain permits, and simultaneously declare the conflict on tower frequency. Do not decelerate back to the runway surface, as this would place you directly in the path of landing traffic. Announce your position and action to ATC (e.g., 'Tower, [callsign], departing Runway 14, deviating right off runway edge, traffic on final'). Once clear, coordinate with tower for re-sequencing. The key principle is that runway incursion avoidance in this scenario shifts from prevention to immediate conflict resolution — lateral and vertical separation must be established using the helicopter's unique maneuverability. After landing, file an ASDE/ASRS report.

