ificate and a Part 135 certificate or authorization depending on the nature of the operation. (3) Turbine aircraft endorsement — 14 CFR 61.31(g) requires a logbook endorsement from an authorized flight instructor before acting as PIC of a turbine-powered aircraft unless the pilot already holds a type rating for that aircraft. Without this endorsement, flight as PIC is prohibited. (4) Practical familiarity — 14 CFR 91.9 and 91.103 require the PIC to be familiar with all available information concerning the flight, and the operator's insurance and operating limitations may prohibit an unqualified pilot. In summary: no commercial certificate, no turbine endorsement, and the prohibition on compensation all independently bar this flight.
