hs — a potential violation of 14 CFR 91.7 for every flight. Fourth, if you knowingly installed an unapproved part, the logbook entry could constitute falsification of records under 14 CFR 43.9 and expose you to certificate action under 14 CFR 61.59; however, if you reasonably believed the filter was approved, the primary violations would be airworthiness and improper maintenance rather than falsification. The new owner's A&P must remove the unapproved part, install an approved filter with a new oil service, and make the appropriate maintenance record entries before the aircraft can legally fly.
