AI_EDIT	PH.V.C.SK.003	The FAA publishes airport diagrams for airports that meet certain criteria, generally larger airports with complex surface layouts. Current airport diagrams are available in the FAA Chart Supplement (formerly Airport/Facility Directory), on FAA aeronautical chart products, via electronic flight bags (EFBs) using current databases, and through products like Jeppesen chart services. Pilots should always verify the diagram is current before use, as they are updated on a 56-day cycle for printed products.	->	The FAA publishes airport diagrams for airports meeting certain criteria, generally larger or more complex airports. Current airport diagrams are available through the FAA Chart Supplement (56-day cycle), FAA terminal procedures publications (28-day cycle), aeronautical charts, electronic flight bags (EFBs) with current databases, and Jeppesen services. The Chart Supplement is updated on a 56-day cycle; airport diagrams within FAA terminal procedures publications are updated on a 28-day cycle. Pilots must verify the diagram is current before use based on the specific product being used. Reference: AIM 2-3-2; FAA Chart Supplement; FAA terminal procedures publication schedule.
