uest Mode A only (no altitude squawk) or may vector you to suitable airspace for repairs. The downstream risks are serious: ATC may issue incorrect TCAS resolution advisories to nearby aircraft; separation assurance is compromised; in RVSM airspace, a 400-foot error would trigger an immediate ATC response; and terrain alerting in other aircraft may be incorrectly activated or suppressed. You should log this discrepancy and ensure the encoder is inspected before the next flight.
