h TSO-C84 or equivalent standards. Operational differences pilots should know: (a) Verify the replacement agent extinguisher is rated for the specific fire risks on your helicopter and follows AC 20-42D guidance. (b) Operating temperature ranges may differ — check the extinguisher nameplate. (c) The PASS technique remains the same. (d) At high concentrations in enclosed spaces, replacement agents can produce decomposition byproducts that are irritating or toxic — ventilate after use. (e) While no FAA regulation mandates replacement of serviceable Halon 1211 extinguishers, recharging discharged or expired Halon units is becoming logistically difficult and expensive, so proactive transition to approved alternatives is industry best practice.
