The follow-up answer regarding compass turns and latitude-based lead/rollout contains oversimplified and potentially misleading guidance. The statement 'turning TO north — lead by latitude; turning TO south — overshoot by latitude' is a mnemonic that, while sometimes taught, can be confusing and context-dependent. The exact lead/rollout adjustment depends on current latitude, hemisphere, direction of turn, and compass card design. The explanation lacks nuance about magnetic dip angle variation by latitude and does not adequately address the complexity of compass errors during turns.
