The answer conflates Part 135 general requirements (14 CFR 135.181-191) with Category A obstacle clearance standards. While the conclusion is operationally sound, the regulatory citation is imprecise: 135.181-191 address general VFR/IFR operational requirements, not specific obstacle clearance margins. Category A performance rules (if applicable) are found in 14 CFR Part 27 or Part 29 certification standards and operator OpSpecs, not directly in 135.181-191.
The answer suggests 50 feet is inadequate but does not cite a specific minimum margin standard that applies to this scenario. For Category A operations, there are specific takeoff performance requirements in OpSpecs, but the answer does not clearly distinguish between Part 91 (no specific margin) and Part 135 Category A (which has specific requirements depending on the operator's authorization).
The reference to 14 CFR 91.13 (careless/reckless operation) for Part 91 is correct but is a general safety standard, not a specific obstacle clearance regulation.

