nate is required. The proposed alternate at 600 and 2 miles technically meets standard alternate minimums for a precision approach (600 ft ceiling and 2 miles visibility per 14 CFR 91.169(c)(2)), BUT this is the absolute regulatory minimum with zero safety margin. Best practice is to seek an alternate with at least 800-foot ceiling and 3-mile visibility to maintain a safety buffer, especially given the marginal destination weather. Step 4 — Overall: While the alternate technically meets minimums, the combination of marginal destination weather and an alternate at the bare regulatory floor represents elevated risk. Consider NO-GO or replanning for a better alternate.
