ESCALATE	HI.VIII.A.S5.003	The specific altitude tolerance values (±5 feet above 10 feet AGL, implied ±0.5 feet or similar below 10 feet) are stated with confidence but lack independent verification against current FAA-S-ACS-13 or FAA-S-ACS-14; the two-tier tolerance system is plausible but requires confirmation of exact thresholds and values.
