AI_EDIT	HI.XVII.B.S1.001	SRM stands for Single-Pilot Resource Management. It integrates risk management, situational awareness (SA), workload management, controlled flight into terrain (CFIT) awareness, and automation management. During a checkride, a pilot must demonstrate all of these working together — not just one in isolation.	->	CRM stands for Crew Resource Management, adapted for single-pilot operations as Single-Pilot CRM. Three key components a pilot must demonstrate are: (1) Risk Management, (2) Situational Awareness, and (3) Workload Management. These work together to reduce errors and manage flight safely.
