AI_EDIT	HI.XVII.C.K3.002	The FAA recommends visual confirmation in addition to the verbal three-step exchange. The pilot accepting the controls should physically take the controls and the pilot transferring should visually confirm that the accepting pilot has positive control of the aircraft before releasing. This eliminates any ambiguity about who is actually flying.	->	The accepting pilot should physically place hands and feet on the controls during or immediately after the verbal exchange to establish tactile awareness, and the transferring pilot should visually confirm positive control before releasing. This physical/visual confirmation is part of executing the positive exchange protocol, not a separate step, and ensures unambiguous control authority.
