AI_EDIT	HI.XVIII.E.S1.003	Lateral cyclic (into the slope) is the primary control used. As the upslope skid contacts the ground first, the pilot applies cyclic toward the slope to hold the upslope skid firmly on the terrain while slowly reducing collective to lower the downslope skid to the ground. This prevents the helicopter from sliding or rolling away from the slope.	->	Lateral cyclic (away from the slope / toward the upslope side) is the primary control used. As the downslope skid contacts the ground first, the pilot applies cyclic toward the upslope side to prevent the helicopter from rolling downhill while slowly reducing collective to lower the upslope skid to the ground. This prevents dynamic rollover and maintains lateral control throughout the landing sequence.
AI_EDIT	HI.XVIII.E.S1.005	Lifting both skids simultaneously on a slope risks the helicopter drifting downhill and losing lateral control before adequate altitude is gained, and it bypasses the controlled transition that prevents dynamic rollover. The correct technique is to apply collective smoothly while holding the upslope skid on the ground with lateral cyclic into the slope. As the helicopter's weight shifts to the downslope skid, continue applying collective until the downslope skid lifts, then the upslope skid follows and the aircraft rises into a level hover. This controlled sequence prevents abrupt lateral displacement and keeps the pilot in authority throughout the transition.	->	Lifting both skids simultaneously on a slope risks the helicopter drifting downhill and losing lateral control before adequate altitude is gained, and it bypasses the controlled transition that prevents dynamic rollover. The correct technique is to apply collective smoothly while holding the upslope skid firmly on the ground with lateral cyclic into the slope. As collective is increased, the downslope skid (being lower) will lift first. Continue applying collective and maintain upslope cyclic authority until the downslope skid clears the terrain, then as additional collective is applied, the upslope skid lifts and the aircraft transitions into a stable hover. This controlled sequence prevents lateral drift downslope and maintains cyclic authority throughout the transition.
