Under 14 CFR 91.107, the PIC is required to ensure each occupant has their safety belt properly secured during movement on the surface, takeoff, and landing. If a passenger refuses, the PIC's only compliant option is to not move the aircraft until the passenger complies, or to remove the noncompliant passenger from the flight. Departing with an unsecured passenger during taxi is a direct violation of 91.107 by the PIC, regardless of whether the passenger consented. The PIC cannot delegate this responsibility — the FAA holds the PIC accountable, and a violation could result in certificate action.

