The follow-up answer regarding semirigid rotors and mast bumping is accurate but somewhat tangential to the core question about Coriolis effects during low RPM. While mast bumping is a valid concern with semirigid rotors at low G, it is not directly an aerodynamic consequence of low RPM itself.
